A click below the text of an element, with a closer line outside the
element, puts Ladybird’s selection caret on the element’s own closest
line. Blink, WebKit and Gecko all look for the caret position in the
content of the element the point hits: Blink’s PhysicalBoxFragment::
PositionForPointInBlockFlowDirection() and WebKit’s RenderBlock::
positionForPoint() take the hit block’s last child for a point below
all of it, and Gecko’s nsIFrame::GetContentOffsetsFromPoint() drills
down to the closest frame inside the hit frame. So the click selects
at the end of the element’s text, rather than leaving the selection
where it was; Chrome puts the caret there in a manual check.
